<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ishpakai</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 675 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ishpakai was the earliest known Scythian king, named in Assyrian texts from the reign of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esarhaddon">Esarhaddon</a> as ruler of Ishkuza in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>. He allied with the Mannaeans against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a> and was killed in battle with the Assyrians around 675 BCE. He is sometimes considered the predecessor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bartatua">Bartatua</a>.</p></div>
